# SYNOPSIS

```usage
ucdgen datadir output.swift
```

# DESCRIPTION

`ucdgen` reads the Unicode Character Database's files from <datadir> (`data/unicode` in the tree) and writes the tables TDUnicode searches: canonical combining classes, decompositions, compositions, case folding and uppercasing to <output.swift>, and the grapheme, word and line break properties to `SegmentationTables.swift` beside it.
It runs on the dev machine and is built by SwiftPM (`.build/debug/ucdgen`).
The tree's copies are in `text/unicode/lib/generated`, and UnicodeTests fails when they differ from what `ucdgen` would write.

It reads `UnicodeData.txt`, `CompositionExclusions.txt`, `CaseFolding.txt` and `SpecialCasing.txt` for the first, and `GraphemeBreakProperty.txt`, `WordBreakProperty.txt`, `LineBreak.txt`, `DerivedCoreProperties.txt`, `EastAsianWidth.txt` and `emoji-data.txt` for the second.
Normalization follows UAX #15, case folding takes CaseFolding's full mappings (statuses C and F), and uppercasing takes UnicodeData's simple mappings, replaced by SpecialCasing's unconditional ones.
Each table is sorted, for a binary search.
The outputs say they are generated and not to be edited.
It prints `ucdgen: Unicode <version>: <n> decompositions, <n> composites, <n> foldings`.

# EXAMPLES

After new UCD files are copied into `data/unicode`:

```rc
% .build/debug/ucdgen data/unicode text/unicode/lib/generated/Tables.swift
```

